  "headSHASemantics": "This is the last integrated implementation and CI head covered by the inventory. Commits after it change only evidence pins and wording; the live HTTP/WSS positive control remains explicitly opt-in and is not claimed as an ordinary CI pass.",
  "scope": "WebView package-resource security boundary, ephemeral WebKit session lifecycle, per-session capability-bound input.read, navigation policy, actual WebKit provenance checks, isolated-world reply delivery, bounded replay state, trusted external-link activation contracts, package/version-scoped installed-renderer safe mode, the SwiftUI installed-renderer host and Source fallback, per-session storage and file-isolation coverage, and a live HTTP plus trusted-TLS WebSocket positive-control harness. The bridge has closed methods, bounded envelopes and payloads, replay rejection, main-frame and webView/origin/session checks, exact version-pinned source and markdown reads, and an isolated-world postMessage relay. Trusted activation uses a short-lived, one-use cryptographic nonce bound to a normalized HTTP(S) destination and host context. Failure accounting stores only a package identity, a closed cause, and a timestamp. The hosted WSS control uses a login-keychain identity with SHA-1 7C0B00954A876487620BE7B2E2D0FDEC54B8EF08 when its explicit hosted-network gate is enabled. It does not claim a pass when disabled.",
  "ciCoverage": "ordinary CI runs the selected portable WebKit-facing suites: package scheme handler, content-world bridge, external activation redemption gate, and SwiftUI host/session lifecycle. RendererSessionIsolationTests and RendererHostedWebKitHarnessTests do not run in ordinary CI because they require real GUI/WebKit storage or hosted network and login-keychain prerequisites.",
  "futureInputContract": "RendererAuthorizedInputReader receives version-pinned SourceVersionID source bytes or SourceMarkdownVersionID processed Markdown. It must not call live sourceContent(id:) for session input.",
