  "honestCoverageLimits": [
    "The portable provider tests do not run a live WKWebView or prove general network isolation. The later hosted network harness owns that claim.",
    "The opt-in lifecycle tests do not load a live renderer document. A later hosted network harness owns end-to-end WebKit behavior.",
    "The SwiftUI host tests mount a real WKWebView only through a recording session. They prove insertion, deferred lifecycle ordering, failure deferral, replacement teardown, and Source fallback dispatch; they do not prove a live package navigation.",
    "The session-isolation tests exercise real ephemeral WebKit data stores and file-navigation rejection. They do not prove the general network-isolation matrix.",
    "The portable isolated-world bridge tests exercise handler routing, reply encoding, and injected provenance. They do not run a live renderer document or prove WebKit supplies that provenance. A hosted suite still owns that claim.",
    "The bridge and navigation tests do not prove live frame identity, navigation cancellation, or network isolation. A hosted WebKit suite must cover those conditions.",
    "The trusted-activation contract and redemption-gate tests do not execute a live WKWebView. They do not prove that WebKit supplies the observed provenance or that synthetic page events cannot obtain a nonce. The source-contract test checks that the nonce does not cross a shared window message path.",
    "The command-entry seam proves a successful invocation returns to async @main. It does not invoke LocalGit or GitHubCLI against a live pull request.",
    "The trusted-TLS WebSocket positive control runs only when WIKIFS_RENDERER_HOSTED_NETWORK_TESTS=1 and the supplied login-keychain identity is available. It reports a disabled diagnostic when either prerequisite is absent. It does not run in ordinary CI, does not claim a pass when disabled, and does not prove restrictive network isolation."
  ]
}
